 "about": "The owner's Chrome relay (docs/chrome.md, \"Steps\"): planque's signed steps, one per op, the extension's signed answers (a page, a refusal, a hand-over handed) and the person's answers to a hand-over. Each message has its label, its body, the exact bytes signed (label, a zero byte, the body's JCS) and a signature that verifies under the key named. The extension (chrome/test/vectors.test.js) and planque (its vendored copy, testdata/chrome-relay.json) read the same file. A step travels as {type: \"step\", step, sig}; an answer as {type, ...body, sig}, so neither can sign or check a field the other doesn't.",
